  "part": {
    "name": "Exploded modular hotend and heater-block assembly",
    "description": "Nine-solid mechanical assembly comprising two manifold or heat-sink bodies, two heater or clamp blocks, a support carriage, a tubular heat break, and three interchangeable threaded nozzle or fitting variants. Visible functional features include stepped mounting bores, cross-passages, split clamp slots, heat-dissipation fins, threaded interfaces, hex wrench flats, internal flow passages, chamfers, and stress-relieving corner blends. STEP face assignments are based on face geometry, bounding boxes, axes, areas, and correspondence with the labeled views.",
    "source_views": [
      "front",
      "back",
      "left",
      "right",
      "top",
      "bottom",
      "toprightiso"
    ],
    "symmetry_note": "Most individual components exhibit bilateral or rotational symmetry about their principal bore axes. The finned heat sink is approximately symmetric left-to-right but is interrupted by side holes and front-to-back fin geometry. The clamp and heater blocks are asymmetric because of slots, cross-holes, and offset mounting holes. The three nozzle or fitting components are rotationally symmetric above their hexagonal wrench sections."
